  "body": "The caption browser used three fixed 100 ms pauses before handling confirmation dialogs. An older duplicate CI run received \u201cNo dialog is showing,\u201d then never completed its unbounded diagnostic evaluation. The test now arms a fresh exact-confirm waiter before each click, bounds CDP requests and diagnostics, drains pending requests on close/error, and awaits owned child shutdown before removing the private browser profile. All original cancel/discard, review, reopen, export and narrow-layout assertions remain intact; product and workflow files are unchanged.\n\nAt `abbae728434fa0670478e12216a1d94603a97daf`, independent syntax checks and the controlled protocol regression pass. The regression reproduces the old failure with a 180 ms dialog delay and covers delayed cancel/accept, absent/wrong dialogs, trigger failures, request expiry, late replies and socket drainage. The existing caption CI entrypoint runs these checks before its real browser fixture.\n\nThe complete PostgreSQL 17.6 / Chromium 151 caption journey also passed with exact source-file hashes matching this commit: three observed decisions false/true/true, all original assertions, four-record ZIP and 390 px layout. Both registered test schemas were removed and queried absent; owned child exits preceded temporary removal. The receipt was generated before committing, so its source_commit identifies the base HEAD; the recorded modified-file hashes establish the tested source. The existing generation provider is a controlled fixture, with no model-quality or training claim. Full evidence, original cancelled-run disposition and diagnosis limits are in docs/plans/lab-workflow-reliability/reports/caption-dialog-ci-20261020.\n\nCurrent composed head `0dedbc953902ac89389dca0693006aaa02a0a87c` follows PR111 at exact base `29011daea37f101ee30be9bc10aab702a16c830a`. A normal whole-history merge carries the independently reviewed project-startup readiness fix; product bytes exactly match PR111, and both caption and startup qualification file hashes remain equal to their original tested snapshots. The two focused regressions and syntax checks also pass on the composed tree. Hosted acceptance and serial integration remain pending. The original duplicate is cancelled, never counted as passing; its newer independently reviewed same-head primary remains the PR105 acceptance gate.\n",
